      "description": "Led efforts in writing HTML, CSS, and Javascript to perform A/B tests on Dell.com to enable data-driven decision-making for changes to Dell.com design/functionality while working with designers and product owners to ensure A/B tests are feasible and consistent with the design system.\nRecognized by senior management for developing A/B tests 50% faster than average and maintaining quality while working primarily on high complexity tests, typically involving significant page redesign, multiple API calls, and responsive design.\nPromoted to Senior Software Engineer from Software Engineer II for consistently exceeding expectations. The promotion included new Dev Lead responsibilities such as mentoring and assisting other team members, evaluating teammates and their progress, and continuously providing new ideas to improve the team output and processes.\nParticipated with Adobe Target implementation and maintenance across Dell.com, which included updating code, managing cookie consent, adjusting for different application architecture, and writing profile scripts to bring personalized experiences to the Dell website.\nDeveloped and maintained Chrome Extensions and a JavaScript bookmarklet that enhanced internal testing tools and workflows.\nServed as an interim Focal Point, managing Adobe Target activities, offers, and audiences, and coordinating with optimization managers on test launches and completions in addition to regular responsibilities.\nProvided front-end development expertise to internal engineering teams, collaborating to implement feature enhancements on Dell.com using .NET Core, ensuring seamless integration and optimized performance.",
